const e="k-days-talent-search",u=2023,t="Built from the 2023 K-Days Talent Search Rules and Regulations. The document prints no venue, no semi-final or final dates, no prize amounts, no ranks or points and no contact names or phone numbers, so those parts are empty. Its dates mix years: open audition entries are printed as due 25 May 2022 and video entries 9 June 2023; both are kept as printed. Rule numbering skips rule 15. Group size limits are printed inconsistently (Youth 'eight (9)', Adult 'six (9)'); the printed words and figures are both given. The final's scoring (60 technique, 30 showmanship, 10 interview) differs from the semi-final's (60/40); the template installs the semi-final criteria.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"K-Days Talent Search (Explore Edmonton). Read these rules before you enter.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Entries need the fee: {{AdminFee}}. Video entries close on {{VideoEntryDeadline}} at 4 p.m. Acts may not be longer than {{MaxActTime}}. Be at the venue: {{ArrivalTime}}.",Notes:["The semi-finals and the final are held during K-Days. Dates: {{EventDates}}.","The printed document says open audition entries were due on {{OpenAuditionDeadline}}; this date is from the 2022 edition and is kept as printed.","Contact the organiser by e-mail: {{EntryEmail}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The competition is for amateur performers in three age divisions: Junior, Youth and Adult.","Acts are entered through a video audition or an open audition. The best acts go to the semi-finals and then to the final.","The K-Days Talent Search Committee and Explore Edmonton Corporation (EEC) make the final decision on all matters.","They may change, alter or rearrange parts or all of these rules at any time.","By entering a video or an open audition, performers give EEC the right to photograph, film and sound record their performance at the Talent Search and at K-Days. EEC may use these for advertising, promotion and trade in newspapers and other publications, radio and television, film releases and interactive media worldwide, with no further payment or permission.","Performers waive all moral rights in their performance and in the submitted materials. They agree to hold EEC harmless from claims about publicity rights, defamation, invasion of privacy, copyright, trade-mark or other intellectual property.","By entering an audition, performers also let EEC (or its agents) use, print, publish and reproduce their personal information, pictures and recordings, including name, voice, statements and any video or sound recording, for any purpose, with no further payment or permission."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Performers must be residents of Alberta.","Employees, volunteers and immediate family of Explore Edmonton Corporation (EEC) and of the other organisations involved are not eligible to perform.","Junior Division: the performer must be {{JuniorAgeTest}}.","Youth Division: the performer must be {{YouthAgeTest}}.","Adult Division: the performer must be {{AdultAgeTest}}.","The average age of the members of a multi-member act decides the division the act performs in.","The competition is open to all amateur performers only.","An amateur may not earn more than 50 per cent of their annual taxable salary from performing.","An amateur may not have signed a management or booking agreement with a professional organisation that is, or will be, paid a fee for securing work in the entertainment field. A professional organisation is any management company with more than one full-time staff member.","An amateur may not have a current recording contract with a major, national or multi-national recording and publishing company such as Sony/BMG, Warner, EMI or Universal.","A performer who has already won a place in the semi-finals through one open audition may not compete in a second open audition.","A member of a divisional winning act may not perform in the same age division in later K-Days Talent Search competitions."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Open audition: submit the entry and application form to EEC with the fee ({{AdminFee}}). Use the online application form to sign up before the open auditions; registration is needed before going on stage. Complete entry information and the fee must be in by {{OpenAuditionDeadline}}, or the performer is not eligible to compete.","Video audition: the application form and video must reach EEC by 4 p.m. on {{VideoEntryDeadline}}, with the fee. Forms that arrive without the fee, late, incomplete or hard to read are not accepted.","A video entry must show an amateur performance recorded within the last 12 months. One performance is allowed per online entry.","YouTube video entries are accepted and encouraged.","Put the act's name and contact information on every video label, and include complete entry information and the fee with the video.","Film in a well-lit area. Make sure the background music does not drown out the vocal performance. Watch the video before you submit it. Extra audio equipment is not recommended.","There is no limit to the number of auditions (video or open) a performer may submit and attend. The fee applies to each performer with each submission.","Send the music accompaniment in electronic form only, by e-mail to {{EntryEmail}}, before your audition and competition date.","Also bring a backup track on a smartphone or USB stick, in case the player cannot read the original. For an open audition, bring a backup with a second option if the first is not compatible.","Send the lyrics of your music to {{EntryEmail}} before the semi-finals."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["The administration fee is {{AdminFee}}.","The fee must be paid with every audition entry, and it is paid for each performer in a group act.","All administration fees are non-refundable."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["Video audition entries close at 4 p.m. on {{VideoEntryDeadline}}.","Open audition entries and fee close on {{OpenAuditionDeadline}} (as printed).","Semi-finals and the final: {{EventDates}}.","Be present at least 60 minutes before show time on your scheduled competition date. Acts that are not present before show time may be disqualified."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Rounds and Qualification",Items:["Round 1: video and open auditions. At least twelve winners from each age division, from both audition types, move to the semi-finals during K-Days.","Round 2: semi-finals in each division. Three winners and one wild card selected by the committee from each division's semi-final go to the final.","Final: 12 acts compete in total.","All division finalists may perform in one act in the final. If a performer qualifies in two separate acts, they must choose which act to perform in the final. The next highest scoring act in that division is then drawn to compete.","Each act that reaches the final must also attend an impromptu session, a 10-minute interview."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["Semi-final performances: judges score 60 percent technique and 40 percent showmanship, a maximum total of 100 percent.","Final performances: judges score 60 percent technique and 30 percent showmanship. The 10-minute impromptu interview is the remaining 10 percent of the total score.","Questions or comments go to the Northlands organisers.","No verbal contact is allowed between performers, their representatives and the judges at any level of the program. Failure to comply may lead to disqualification."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct and Disqualification",Items:["Any performance that is not suited for a family audience is disqualified.","Explicit language, swearing, or suggestive lyrics or actions lead to disqualification.","Live animals, machetes, knives, fire and pyrotechnics are not accepted.","No object used in an act may be thrown off the stage.","Accompanists agree to follow the rules and regulations. Accompaniments are the sole responsibility of the performer."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes and Winner Commitments",Items:["The printed rules name no prize amounts.","If EEC asks, the divisional winning acts must make at least two appearances for the K-Days Talent Search Committee and EEC between July of the current year and July of the next year, when and as EEC says.","EEC is not obliged to ask the winning acts to make these appearances."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Group Acts and Accompaniment",Items:["Group size limits as printed: {{GroupSizeLimits}}.","Accompaniment is allowed in all categories but must be true accompaniment. It means extra people on stage, up to a maximum of three, and the total number must not exceed the number allowed in the category.","The accompaniment must not become visually or musically more important than the act. The test is whether the act can stand alone without it."]}],Documents:[{Title:"K-Days Talent Search Rules and Regulations 2023 (PDF)",Url:"https://assets-global.website-files.com/622a8f685d728511ae53ced4/63fe4b8ef499006affe45024_Talent%20Search%20Rules%20and%20Regulations%202023.pdf"}]},a=[],i=[{AgeGroup:"Junior Solo",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(A)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Performer must be {{JuniorAgeTest}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Performer must be {{JuniorAgeTest}}.`},{AgeGroup:"Youth Solo",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(B)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Performer must be {{YouthAgeTest}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Performer must be {{YouthAgeTest}}.`},{AgeGroup:"Adult Solo",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(C)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Performer must be {{AdultAgeTest}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Performer must be {{AdultAgeTest}}.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Group",Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 1(A), 1(D), 2(A)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The average age of the act's members must be in the Junior range: {{JuniorAgeTest}}.","The maximum number of performers is nine (9)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The average age of the act's members must be in the Junior range: {{JuniorAgeTest}}.
- The maximum number of performers is nine (9).`},{AgeGroup:"Youth Group",Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 1(B), 1(D), 2(B)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The average age of the act's members must be in the Youth range: {{YouthAgeTest}}.","The maximum number of performers is printed as 'eight (9)'. The words and the figure disagree."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The average age of the act's members must be in the Youth range: {{YouthAgeTest}}.
- The maximum number of performers is printed as 'eight (9)'. The words and the figure disagree.`},{AgeGroup:"Adult Group",Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 1(C), 1(D), 2(C)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The average age of the act's members must be in the Adult range: {{AdultAgeTest}}.","The maximum number of performers is printed as 'six (9)'. The words and the figure disagree."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The average age of the act's members must be in the Adult range: {{AdultAgeTest}}.
- The maximum number of performers is printed as 'six (9)'. The words and the figure disagree.`}],o=[{Title:"Talent Act",Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 4, 5, 11, 13",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["An act may not be longer than {{MaxActTime}}.","The act is timed from the first sound (live or recorded) or movement, and includes all musical introductions and tags.","Acts over the time limit at the semi-final and final are penalised."],Rules:["Acts are vocal, instrumental, dance or variety. A variety act must follow all the rules of the categories it combines.","Vocal acts: recorded background vocals are allowed.","Instrumental acts: no instrument of the same kind may be used as accompaniment, live or recorded.","Dance acts: the accompaniment, live or recorded, must not have any taps or tap effects that could improve the performance."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Semi-final: 60 percent technique and 40 percent showmanship (total 100).","Final: 60 percent technique, 30 percent showmanship and 10 percent for the impromptu interview."],Points:null,Notes:["Winners are chosen by age division, not by act type."]},Markdown:`## Time and format
- An act may not be longer than {{MaxActTime}}.
- The act is timed from the first sound (live or recorded) or movement, and includes all musical introductions and tags.
- Acts over the time limit at the semi-final and final are penalised.

## Rules
- Acts are vocal, instrumental, dance or variety. A variety act must follow all the rules of the categories it combines.
- Vocal acts: recorded background vocals are allowed.
- Instrumental acts: no instrument of the same kind may be used as accompaniment, live or recorded.
- Dance acts: the accompaniment, live or recorded, must not have any taps or tap effects that could improve the performance.

## Judging
- Semi-final: 60 percent technique and 40 percent showmanship (total 100).
- Final: 60 percent technique, 30 percent showmanship and 10 percent for the impromptu interview.

## Notes for participants
- Winners are chosen by age division, not by act type.`}],r=[],s=[{Key:"EntryEmail",Kind:"contact",Label:"Entry, music and lyrics e-mail",Value:{Name:"K-Days Talent Search",Role:"Music tracks, lyrics and enquiries (organiser's event address)",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"kdaystalentsearch@exploreedmonton.com"},Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 6, 8 and Open Auditions 3"},{Key:"AdminFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Administration fee",Value:"$30 per performer, per submission, non-refundable",Source:"Rules and Regulations rules 2 and 7"},{Key:"VideoEntryDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for video audition entries (received by 4 p.m.)",Value:"2023-06-09",Source:"Rules and Regulations Video Entries 1"},{Key:"OpenAuditionDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for open audition entries and fee (printed as 25 May 2022)",Value:"2022-05-25",Source:"Rules and Regulations Open Auditions 1 and 2"},{Key:"MaxActTime",Kind:"text",Label:"Longest act",Value:"4 minutes 30 seconds",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 4"},{Key:"JuniorAgeTest",Kind:"text",Label:"Junior age test",Value:"5 years old by 1 July and not over 12 years old by 31 July of the current year",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(A)"},{Key:"YouthAgeTest",Kind:"text",Label:"Youth age test",Value:"13 years old by 1 July and not over 18 years old as of 31 July of the current year",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(B)"},{Key:"AdultAgeTest",Kind:"text",Label:"Adult age test",Value:"19 years of age (printed: 'by 19 years of age by the current year')",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 1(C)"},{Key:"GroupSizeLimits",Kind:"text",Label:"Maximum performers in a group act",Value:"Junior nine (9); Youth 'eight (9)'; Adult 'six (9)' (the words and figures disagree in the printed rules)",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 2(A)-(C)"},{Key:"ArrivalTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Be present before show time",Value:"At least 60 minutes before show time on your scheduled competition date",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 10"},{Key:"EventDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Semi-final and final dates",Value:"Not printed (semi-finals and the final are held during K-Days)",Source:"Rules and Regulations rule 12"}],l=[{Claim:"All rules, dates, fees and contacts are taken from the organiser's own 2023 rules document.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"K-Days Talent Search Rules and Regulations 2023 (Explore Edmonton)",Url:"https://assets-global.website-files.com/622a8f685d728511ae53ced4/63fe4b8ef499006affe45024_Talent%20Search%20Rules%20and%20Regulations%202023.pdf"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2023,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,u as Year,d as default};
